ng{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuding/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuding/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuding/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuding/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuding/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuding/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuding/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-03-10T18:40:54Z","updated_at":"2021-03-10T19:15:50Z","body":"With some further investigation I found that it's related to PNG with _grayscale and alpha_. \r\n\r\n```\r\n› file WCcL3Ip.png\r\nWCcL3Ip.png: PNG image data, 36 x 36, 8-bit gray+alpha, non-interlaced\r\n```\r\n\r\nOpened an issue for Squoosh (GoogleChromeLabs/squoosh#971). A temporary work around is to avoid using `gray+alpha` PNGs. When it's `8-bit/color RGBA` it will be handled correctly again. \r\n\r\nRelated: http://www.libpng.org/pub/png/book/chapter08.html#png.ch08.div.5.4. [These images](http://www.simplesystems.org/users/glennrp/png_bugs/gray-alpha/) can also reproduce the bug.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/comments/795889426/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"shuding","id":3676859,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NzY4NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3676859?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuding","html_url":"https://github.com/shuding","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuding/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuding/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuding/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.c